Article 51

1. The Regional Indonesian Child Protection Commission as referred to in Article 45 letter e has detailed tasks including:a. supervising the implementation of protection and fulfillment of children's rights;
b. providing input and proposals in the formulation of policies regarding the implementation of child protection;
c. collecting data and information regarding child protection; d. receiving and conducting reviews of public complaints regarding violations of children's rights;
e. conducting mediation on disputes regarding violations of children's rights; f. cooperating with institutions established by the community in the field of child protection; andg. other tasks in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
2. In the event of changes to laws and regulations concerning the Regional Indonesian Child Protection Commission, the regulation regarding the Regional Indonesian Child Protection Commission shall be guided by laws and regulations which are further regulated by Regent's Regulation.

Article 18

